From: LPM Linux Toolchain Team <toolchain@lpm-linux.invalid>
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] x86: raise znver4 and znver5 branch misprediction cost

Backport the AMD-authored GCC tuning change posted in August 2026.  A larger
misprediction scale makes if-conversion account for the deeper Zen 4 and Zen 5
pipelines instead of treating an unpredictable branch as nearly free.

This is deliberately kept separate from the experimental Zen 2/3 change.

---
 gcc/config/i386/x86-tune-costs.h | 4 ++--
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/gcc/config/i386/x86-tune-costs.h b/gcc/config/i386/x86-tune-costs.h
--- a/gcc/config/i386/x86-tune-costs.h
+++ b/gcc/config/i386/x86-tune-costs.h
@@ -2234 +2234 @@ struct processor_costs znver4_cost = {
-  COSTS_N_INSNS (2),			/* Branch mispredict scale.  */
+  COSTS_N_INSNS (2) + 3,		/* Branch mispredict scale.  */
@@ -2402 +2402 @@ struct processor_costs znver5_cost = {
-  COSTS_N_INSNS (2),			/* Branch mispredict scale.  */
+  COSTS_N_INSNS (2) + 3,		/* Branch mispredict scale.  */
-- 
2.50.1
